Yes I do, it's where I pull my data from. I maintain four nodes each running instances of Bitcoin Research Kit ontop for redundancy and to enable version control.

It actually highlights that you confounded three different ideas and don't realise it.

- There is no link between being against 110 and being pro-ossification (just being anti retarded and unaceptable soft fork).
- The claim of 'well funded' is confusing 'people who can think critically and technically' for 'financed and against us'.
- Ossification has nothing to do with UTXO set bloat.

This notion that the 110ers have that Bitcoin is a node democracy is just embarassing. I don't have four votes mate, this isn't how Bitcoin works.

If I wanted to undermine BTC you know how I would do it? I would manufacture an endless swamp of nonsense that has no end that keeps all the developers bogged down in a useless social fight.

I would seek to brain drain the protocol by brainwashing goobers with no technical understanding of fork logic or how consensus works to march with pitchforks.

I might even roll out a 'temporary soft fork' that keeps the space arguing over utter nonsense that cannnot be fixed no matter how hard you try.

